       "items": [
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<h3><span style=\"color: #008080;\">San Carlos Turns 100</span></h3>",
         "look": {
          "m": {
           "ta": "center"
          },
          "h3": {
           "s": 39,
           "ta": "center"
          }
         }
        },
        {
         "t": "divider"
        },
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">July 8, 2025</h2>\n<p>With only 600 residents, a small schoolhouse, and one incredible man, Ed Wheeler, who served as both the police and fire departments, San Carlos took charge of its own future and officially became a city in July 8, 1925. San Carlos officially celebrates its 100th year birthday this 2025.</p>",
         "look": {
          "b": {
           "s": 16
          }
         }
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "rows": [
    {
     "cols": [
      {
       "w": "4/4",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span class=\"blue\">MEMORY WALL</span></h3>",
         "look": {
          "h3": {
           "s": 39
          }
         }
        },
        {
         "t": "divider"
        },
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\">San Carlos is turning 100, and we’re inviting you to help us build a Memory Wall to celebrate! Share a photo, a story, a sweet message to a neighbor, or even a funny moment from around town. It’s a chance to reflect, connect, and show what makes San Carlos feel like home, one memory at a time.</p>",
         "look": {
          "b": {
           "s": 16
          }
         }
        },
        {
         "t": "button",
         "text": "Share A Story",
         "href": "#shareamemory"
        },
        {
         "t": "button",
         "text": "Share A Photo",
         "href": "#shareaphoto"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
